This is my fifth or so ascension, and second wizard.  After taking a
year+ break, I was going to start up a new game, but spotted an
unfinished game, Wizzy.

He was at the end of last year's nethack spree, and was about 1,000
turns into it.  Seemed like a pretty lucky guy, as he started out with
a magic marker and a scroll of charging, as well as magic missile as
his 2nd spell.  All he had done was have his pet loot a potion shop.
There were a lot of altars in this game, 3 aligned, one of which had a
priest.

I played him fast and loose(as I tend to do), and he got into some
pretty deep trouble in the mines, as well as the mazes.  He was chased
down by ants and other nasties.  I have no clue how he survived, but
there was a lot of dancing and running, hoping that magic would
regenerate and the spells would hit.

For some reason I found a lot of tripe and lots of dogs and cats.
Managed to find a polymorph trap, but the best I could muster was an
ape.  Eventually I managed to gain enough levels and push skill up
with quarterstaff to be useful.  I foolishly repeatedly ate things
trying to gain poison resistance, but with no luck, just drained
strength.  I had a nasty run in with a winged gargoyle and other
baddies and somehow had the sense to zap them away(I'm learning,
finally).  I managed to find 2 more magic markers, and I was able to
write a book of identify.... which I used the heck out of.

Big break came on about dlvl 10 or so.  From the stairs, all I spotted
was a lamp(first one in the game).  It was magical.  With all the
altars, I had no problem getting water and getting the lamp blessed.
Wished for SDSM.  From then on it just got better.  Sacrificed for
Magicbane, also got Sting.  I trained up on daggers.  Managed to get
the resistances I needed and a BoH from Sokoban.  More sacrifices
later and I was given stealth, speed, protection, and about half a
dozen spellbooks.  Never could get crowned...

I would like to mention at this point that I ran into multiple
laprechaun halls, as well as tons of beehives, throne rooms etc.  This
was a big source of gold, food, and items for me.

I used gold detection to raid vaults and buy 10AC.  I later did
Ludios, but I didn't know what to do with 60K gold.  I just donated it
all and had nothing to show for it.  To make things worse, I fell in
the moat and ruined some good scrolls and potions.  Somwhere along the
way I picked up free action, conflict, and slow digestion rings.

Did the quest, and found gauntlets of dexterity.  I foolishly ate a
Tengu and got teleportitis(I thought they only conveyed control).  I
was teleported into the moat on the quest.  Luckily I had just found a
magic breathing amulet on the same level(which I wore most of the
game).  Quest wasn't too bad.  After that, with the regeneration, I
was casting willy-nilly.  Worked spells up to at least basic, and
attack even further.

At this point, it started getting silly.  Medusa had another magic
lamp, never used it.  Rampaged the castle, and got a fully charged
wand.  I was planning on wishing for missing armor, as that is how
most of my ascesions work out.  For ONCE, I had the sense to check the
armory first.  Found helm of brilliance, speed boots, and some other
good boots as well, which I just left.  Valley of the dead almost
immediately turned up gauntlets of power, which I saved, but never
used.  Also found another tengu corpse and got teleport control.  I
enchanted my gear up with the last of my markers and foo-proofed
them.  Also, I genocided 'L' and ';'.  Some earlier thrones yielded
genocides for disenchanters and master mind flayers.  I ended up
burning a wish for another marker, just for good measure.  I ended up
writing a book of magic mapping, a scroll of charging, and some gold
detection scrolls for the planes.

I moved swiftly from there, finding a few wands of death(including
Orcus).  I payed off two demons.  Found Vlad's tower.  Best Vlad loot
ever.  Found two life saving amulets, and put one on to replace my
magical breathing. Found at least half a dozen spellbooks.  Finally,
one of the chests had a full charged wishing wand(which i never
touched).
At this point, I was getting nervous that the RNG was planning a fun
ending.

I had dug up all my paths and marked the square, so I just went for it
at that point.  First problem seemed to be that my wands of death were
chronically missing the Rodney.  After some jostling, I finally killed
him, and made for the square.  The priests were as annoying as usual.
After another Rodney run-in, I realized that the death wands weren't
going to cut it.  I wished for a blessed spellbook of finger of
death.  Turned out to be a much better wish than I thought, and I used
it liberally.

The mysterious force wasn't too bad.  Made it most of the way up, and
ran into Yeenoghu.  Ahhh, the RNG is ready for some payback.  It was
on a level where the stairs were far apart, and I did not know that
the amulet did not always block teleport. I tricked him off of the
stairs and beat him into submission.  Next level up, about 100 turns
later.... Demogorgon.  I have never seen him before and was not
prepared.  In desperation, I wished for a cockatrice corpse and stoned
him.

The planes were quick and painless with the gold detection scrolls.  I
polymorphed a few air elementals to escape quickly.  I entered the
Astral Plane and headed towards Pestilence.  A pesky adventurer
generated an Archon.  Surrounded by the well-equipped adventurer,
Pestilence, and an Archon was a little worrisome, but I managed to zap
Pestilence and beat down the other two.  I remembered the ring of
conflict, which I had never used before.  Made travel a lot easier.
Altar was lawful.  I cleaned up the priests and angels and headed to
the center with Death.  He was off chasing an angel, so I just waltzed
right up to the altar, which was chaotic.

An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...


